# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# None of these are needed by any COPY in docker/Dockerfile.production,
# Dockerfile.backend, or Dockerfile.frontend: every stage runs `npm install`
# and builds from source. Excluding them shrinks the build context from
# multiple GB to a few MB and, critically, stops host artifacts leaking into
# published images.
#
# IMPORTANT: server/prisma/data holds local SQLite databases (dev.db,
# prod.db). Without this exclusion a locally-built image bakes in the
# developer's database, including its users. CI is unaffected (clean
# checkout) but local builds were shipping it. See #395.

# ---- Dependencies (rebuilt inside the image by `npm install`) ----
node_modules
**/node_modules

# ---- Build output (regenerated by `npm run build`) ----
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
coverage
**/coverage
.vite
**/.vite

# ---- Local databases / runtime data (NEVER bake these in) ----
server/prisma/data
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite-journal
**/*.sqlite3-journal

# ---- Secrets & local environment ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# ---- Version control & editor cruft ----
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# ---- Logs & caches ----
*.log
logs
**/.npm
**/.cache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Docs & tests not needed to build ----
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
docs
